Subject: [PATCH 1/2] import NumbaPerformanceWarning from numba.core.errors

The vendored mmdet3d imports `numba.errors`, which numba 0.49 moved to
`numba.core.errors`; the env's numba 0.60 has only the new path, so importing
Bench2DriveZoo's `mmcv` fails before any model is built:

    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'numba.errors'

An import at module scope, so no setting can reach it.

---
diff --git a/mmcv/datasets/pipelines/data_augment_utils.py b/mmcv/datasets/pipelines/data_augment_utils.py
index 231ab80..a5c1c1f 100644
--- a/mmcv/datasets/pipelines/data_augment_utils.py
+++ b/mmcv/datasets/pipelines/data_augment_utils.py
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 import numba
 import numpy as np
 import warnings
-from numba.errors import NumbaPerformanceWarning
+from numba.core.errors import NumbaPerformanceWarning  # uniad_vad: numba>=0.49 moved it
 
 from mmcv.core.bbox import box_np_ops
 
